    "## Thresholds"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5595a607-1c95-4604-842e-0d2ade28331b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "High_stress = stress >= 7  \n",
    "High_anxiety = anxiety >= 7  \n",
    "Poor_diet = diet_quality <= 3  \n",
    "Heavy_sweating = sweating >= 4  "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6933b6fc-555f-4f45-bb30-e219e1dfd50d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Well-known Psychology/Health KPIs Derived from Ratios\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Anxiety-to-Stress Ratio\n",
    "**Formula:** `Anxiety Level / Stress Level`\n",
    "\n",
    "Measures how much anxiety a person experiences relative to their perceived stress. A ratio >1 suggests anxiety is disproportionate to stressors (common in GAD).\n",
    "\n",
    "## 2. Sleep Efficiency Index (proxy)\n",
    "**Formula:** `Sleep Hours / 8`\n",
    "\n",
    "Normalized sleep adequacy score. Values <0.75 are clinically associated with anxiety and mood disorders.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 3. Caffeine-to-Sleep Ratio\n",
    "**Formula:** `Caffeine Intake / Sleep Hours`\n",
    "\n",
    "High caffeine relative to sleep is a known anxiety amplifier. Used in behavioral health screening.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 4. Physical Activity-to-Stress Ratio\n",
    "**Formula:** `Physical Activity / Stress Level`\n",
    "\n",
    "Reflects coping capacity. Higher activity relative to stress = better resilience. Used in lifestyle medicine.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 5. Therapy Engagement Ratio\n",
    "**Formula:** `Therapy Sessions / Anxiety Level`\n",
    "\n",
    "How much therapeutic support someone is receiving per unit of anxiety. Low values flag undertreated cases.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 6. Autonomic Arousal Index\n",
    "**Formula:** `Heart Rate / Breathing Rate`\n",
    "\n",
    "A known physiological ratio. Normal resting ratio ≈ 4:1 (72 bpm / 18 breaths). Elevated values indicate sympathetic nervous system activation (fight-or-flight).\n",
    "\n",
    "## 7. Alcohol-to-Sleep Ratio\n",
    "**Formula:** `Alcohol Consumption / Sleep Hours`\n",
    "\n",
    "Alcohol disrupts sleep architecture; this ratio is used in substance-related anxiety assessment.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 8. Substance Load vs. Diet Quality\n",
    "**Formula:** `(Caffeine Intake + Alcohol Consumption) / Diet Quality`\n",
    "\n",
    "A composite lifestyle burden score — higher values indicate poor health behaviors relative to diet quality.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 9. Stress-to-Coping Ratio\n",
    "**Formula:** `Stress Level / (Physical Activity + Therapy Sessions + 1)`\n",
    "\n",
    "+1 avoids division by zero. Higher = worse coping relative to stressors. Directly maps to the Stress-Coping Balance model in clinical psychology.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "The most psychologically validated of these are **#1 (Anxiety/Stress)**, **#6 (HR/BR)**, and **#9 (Stress-Coping)** — they have direct parallels in clinical assessment literature.\n"
   ]
  },
