  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "efdf2eec",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Numeric vs Categorical Analysis\n",
    "This analysis examines whether there is a statistically significant association between two categorical variables using the Chi-Square Test of Independence.\n",
    "\n",
    "Null Hypothesis (H₀):** The two categorical variables are independent. There is no significant association between them.\n",
    "Alternative Hypothesis (H₁):** The two categorical variables are not independent. There is a significant association between them.\n",
    "If p-value < 0.05, reject the null hypothesis (H₀).\n",
    "If p-value ≥ 0.05, fail to reject the null hypothesis (H₀).\n",
    "\n",
    "- To compare a continuous feature against a binary categorical target, we first assess normality\n",
    "- using the Shapiro-Wilk test. If both groups are normally distributed, we apply an independent\n",
    "- samples t-test. If not, we attempt a Box-Cox transformation to normalize the data and re-test.\n",
    "- If normality still cannot be achieved, we fall back to the non-parametric Mann-Whitney U test."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 102,
   "id": "6663a298",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def numeric_vs_categorical(data, col_1, col_2, alpha=0.05):\n",
    "\n",
    "    numeric_vs_categorical_plot(data, col_1, col_2)\n",
    "\n",
    "    data = data.copy()\n",
    "    data[col_2] = np.where(data[col_2] == 1, 'Yes', data[col_2])\n",
    "    data[col_2] = np.where(data[col_2] == 0, 'No',  data[col_2])\n",
    "\n",
    "    categories_unique = data[col_2].dropna().unique()\n",
    "    X1 = data[data[col_2] == categories_unique[0]][col_1].dropna()\n",
    "    X2 = data[data[col_2] == categories_unique[1]][col_1].dropna()\n",
    "\n",
    "    shapiro_p0 = stats.shapiro(X1).pvalue\n",
    "    shapiro_p1 = stats.shapiro(X2).pvalue\n",
    "    print(f\"Shapiro group 1: p = {shapiro_p0:.4f}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Shapiro group 2: p = {shapiro_p1:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    p = None  \n",
    "\n",
    "    if shapiro_p0 > alpha and shapiro_p1 > alpha:\n",
    "        t, p = stats.ttest_ind(X1, X2)\n",
    "        print(f\"Normal distribution -> t-test\")\n",
    "        print(f\"t = {t:.4f}, p = {p:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            X1_transformed, _ = stats.boxcox(X1 + 1)\n",
    "            X2_transformed, _ = stats.boxcox(X2 + 1)\n",
    "            shapiro_p0_bc = stats.shapiro(X1_transformed).pvalue\n",
    "            shapiro_p1_bc = stats.shapiro(X2_transformed).pvalue\n",
    "\n",
    "            if shapiro_p0_bc > alpha and shapiro_p1_bc > alpha:\n",
    "                t, p = stats.ttest_ind(X1_transformed, X2_transformed)\n",
    "                print(f\"Normal after Box-Cox -> t-test\")\n",
    "                print(f\"t = {t:.4f}, p = {p:.4f}\")\n",
    "            else:\n",
    "\n",
    "                u, p = stats.mannwhitneyu(X1, X2, alternative=\"two-sided\")\n",
    "                print(f\"Not normal after Box-Cox ->> Mann-Whitney\")\n",
    "                print(f\"Statistic = {u:.4f}, p = {p:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "        except Exception:\n",
    "            u, p = stats.mannwhitneyu(X1, X2, alternative=\"two-sided\")\n",
    "            print(f\"Not normal -->> Mann-Whitney\")\n",
    "            print(f\"Statistic = {u:.4f}, p = {p:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    if p is not None:\n",
    "        if p < alpha:\n",
    "            print(f\"Significant difference between '{col_1}' groups\")\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            print(f\"No significant difference between '{col_1}' groups\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7e6b5df5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### compare two categorical\n",
    "This analysis examines whether there is a statistically significant association between two categorical variables using the Chi-Square Test of Independence.\n",
    "- Null Hypothesis (H₀):** The two categorical variables are independent. There is no significant association between them.\n",
    "- Alternative Hypothesis (H₁):** The two categorical variables are not independent. There is a significant association between them.\n",
    "- If **p-value < 0.05**, reject the null hypothesis (H₀).\n",
    "- If **p-value ≥ 0.05**, fail to reject the null hypothesis (H₀)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 103,
   "id": "ac9126a3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def compare_two_categorical(df, col_1, col_2, alpha=0.05):\n",
    "\n",
    "    two_categorical_plot(df, col_1, col_2)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    Data = data.copy()      \n",
    "    Data[col_2] = np.where(Data[col_2] ==1 ,'yes',Data[col_2])\n",
    "    Data[col_2]=  np.where(Data[col_2] ==0,'No', Data[col_2])\n",
    "        \n",
    "    contingency_table = pd.crosstab(Data[col_1],Data[col_2])\n",
    "\n",
    "    chi2_stat, p_value, dof, expected_table = chi2_contingency(contingency_table)\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(f\"chi2_stat: {chi2_stat:.4f}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"p-value: {p_value:.4f}\")\n",
    "        \n",
    "    if p_value < alpha:  \n",
    "        print(\"Reject the Null Hypothesis\")\n",
    "        print(f\"There IS a significant association between '{col_1}' and '{col_2}'.\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(\"Fail to Reject the Null Hypothesis\")\n",
    "        print(f\"There is NO significant association between '{col_1}' and '{col_2}'.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    "
   ]
  },
