  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "622ad8bb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Correlation Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "- In this part, we created a function to calculate the correlation between variables.\n",
    "\n",
    "- First, we checked the correlation between `Target` and numerical columns.\n",
    "- This helped us understand which numerical variables may be related to the target variable.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Then, we checked the correlation between `Stress Level (1-10)` and numerical columns.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Correlation only shows association.\n",
    "- It does not prove that one variable **causes** another."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 436,
   "id": "f9101e15",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def correlation_table(data, numeric_columns, target):\n",
    "\n",
    "    corr_table = pd.DataFrame()\n",
    "\n",
    "    for col in numeric_columns:\n",
    "\n",
    "        corr, p = stats.spearmanr(data[col],data[target])\n",
    "\n",
    "        if p < 0.05:\n",
    "            result = \"Significant\"\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            result = \"Not Significant\"\n",
    "            \n",
    "\n",
    "        corr_table.loc[col, \"correlation\"] = corr\n",
    "        corr_table.loc[col, \"p_value\"] = p\n",
    "        corr_table.loc[col, \"result\"] = result\n",
    "\n",
    "    return corr_table"
   ]
  },
