  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "44f40122",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Normality Test and ANOVA\n",
    "\n",
    "- Before using ANOVA, we checked the normality assumption for each group.\n",
    "- We used the Shapiro-Wilk test to check if the target variable was normally distributed inside each category.\n",
    "\n",
    "- In some cases, the normality test showed that the data was not normally distributed.\n",
    "- However, we still used ANOVA because our dataset has a large sample size.\n",
    "\n",
    "- ANOVA is usually robust when the sample size is large.\n",
    "- This means that small violations of normality are not always a serious problem.\n",
    "\n",
    "- We used ANOVA to compare the mean of a ordinal numerical target across different categorical groups.\n",
    "\n",
    "- For example, we tested whether the average anxiety level was different across:\n",
    "  - occupation groups\n",
    "  - sleep hour groups\n",
    "  - stress level groups\n",
    "  - diet quality groups\n",
    "  - physical activity groups\n",
    "\n",
    "- If the ANOVA p-value is less than 0.05, we consider the difference between groups statistically significant."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 440,
   "id": "a6523ace",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def narmality_test(data, multi_cat_col, target_col):\n",
    "\n",
    "    output = pd.DataFrame()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    for group in data[multi_cat_col].unique():\n",
    "\n",
    "        sample = data[data[multi_cat_col] == group][target_col]\n",
    "\n",
    "        stat, p = stats.shapiro(sample)\n",
    "\n",
    "        if p < 0.05:\n",
    "            result = \"Not Normal\"\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            result = \"Normal\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "        output.loc[group, \"P_value\"] = p\n",
    "        output.loc[group, \"result\"] = result\n",
    "        \n",
    "    return output"
   ]
  },
